Ladybird now clips each CSS mask layer to the curve of its mask-clip
box, as it clips background layers. Blink, WebKit, and Gecko all paint
mask layers with their background fill-layer code, so the same rounded
clip applies to them: Blink’s BoxPainterBase::PaintMaskImages() calls
PaintFillLayers() with the mask layers, and WebKit’s RenderBox::
paintMaskImages() calls BackgroundPainter::paintFillLayers() with them.
In Gecko, PaintMaskSurface() calls the PaintStyleImageLayerWithSC() of
nsCSSRendering, whose GetImageLayerClip() puts the border radii into
the clip it applies to each mask layer.
